  "findings": [
    "The actual full236 compile stopped in Analyze before Verify (verification_runs=0). Its first mixed-order conflict is main block32 instruction7: DropManaged late(l11), span971..979, while current(l7) is newer due to the post-relay Store. The minimal diagnostic model in extracted-main-ops is debugging support, not a safety certificate.",
    "TakeLocal(current) forgets the old age edges. Returning the owner and Store(current) then establishes new late->current edges. No stale old-current edge was retained; merely deleting stale edges cannot fix this failure.",
    "Types still emits static lexical cleanup late->defer Q->current. This differs from the latest actual whole-local Store order.",
    "The same Store age rule exists independently in the pre-existing Analyze and Verify resource checkers. An actual CLI check of the relay reduction with defer removed also fails Analyze with resource closure: cleanup is not reverse successful initialization order. This is not proof that a pre227 binary was executed; it isolates the existing resource path in the current joint candidate.",
    "The minimum relay-free control passes actual Verify once. The relay/defer minimum fails new defer reconstruction; the no-defer relay minimum fails existing resource reconstruction.",
    "Managed and concrete Closure mutable rebinding already use private retained one-field Package shells. Their field replacement is RHS prepare, old field cleanup, transfer prepared value and StorePackageField; shell initialization rank remains fixed. Bare whole Product rebinding currently uses the ordinary Assign Store(local) path instead."
  ],
